# L §6.1 same: "same also joins two rows or movements inside one model, in a version: a movement listed twice counts once,
# and both rows stay listed as evidence (SF-25)"; L §5.3 version items: "identities: same bank[r32] = bank[r31], two rows
# that state one movement (§5.19)". The statement lists one 100.00 PLN payment twice: konto 1 000.00 - 100.00 = 900.00 PLN
# (L §5.19 Booking an observation; L §5.10 bal).
=== m.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source bank_export "wyciąg"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed

version opening_2026
  cite bank_export
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "saldo"

version statement_01
  cite bank_export
  governs 2026-01
  known 2026-02-01
  covers konto
  bank[r31] = (on: 2026-01-12, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to world amount 100.00 PLN) "line 31"
  bank[r32] = (on: 2026-01-12, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to world amount 100.00 PLN) "line 32"
  same bank[r32] = bank[r31]

ask b: bal(konto, 2026-01-31)
=== expect
b: 900.00 PLN
  cut 2026-03-01
